.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH murk-agent 1  "agent " 
.SH NAME
murk\-agent \- Give AI agents scoped, time\-limited access to secrets (experimental)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmurk agent\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Give AI agents scoped, time\-limited access to secrets (experimental)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
murk\-agent\-plan(1)
Emit schema\-only context safe to paste into an AI agent prompt (experimental)
.TP
murk\-agent\-exec(1)
Run a command with strict agent\-safe defaults (experimental)
.TP
murk\-agent\-grant(1)
Mint a scoped ephemeral key that can read only the named secrets (experimental)
.TP
murk\-agent\-init(1)
Mint a scoped grant and print how to run the agent safely (experimental)
.TP
murk\-agent\-ls(1)
List active agent grants and their TTLs (experimental)
.TP
murk\-agent\-revoke(1)
Revoke an agent grant (experimental)
.TP
murk\-agent\-connect(1)
Add `murk mcp` to an AI client\*(Aqs MCP config and mint a scoped grant for it (experimental)
.TP
murk\-agent\-disconnect(1)
Remove murk\*(Aqs entry from an AI editor\*(Aqs MCP config (experimental)
.TP
murk\-agent\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
